    {
      "caption": "Moving the magnet changes the flux",
      "duration_ms": 10000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Push a magnet towards a coil and the flux threading the coil grows; a voltage appears across the coil. Faraday's law sizes it: emf equals minus N times the rate of change of flux — faster push, bigger emf.",
