      "caption": "Misconception: voltage appears while the magnet sits inside",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s5",
      "narration": "It is the change that counts. While the magnet sits still inside the coil, the flux through the coil is perfectly steady and the meter reads zero. Only when the flux grows or shrinks — the magnet moving in or out — does an emf appear.",
